# Intent: Touches on the face toggle mute, vision off and full quiet (owner design 2026-11-13, changed to tap the same day), drawn on the default skin. TAP the mouth = mute on or off, TAP an eye = vision off or on (the eye shuts fully, owner: "tapping eyes should close them, not half close"), TAP the forehead (above and between the eyes) = full quiet on or off. maipai_touch_core.h is plain C: the screen is tiled into edge margins (28 px top, 20 px sides and bottom, where the quick-settings, volume and stop swipes start), forehead, two eyes, mouth and the rest; a touch only counts if the finger stays within 10 px of where it went down, stays in the region it began in, and is a tap (400 ms or less); a touch that begins in an edge margin is never a toggle; anything that strays is a drag. The toggle regions and the margins never start a listen (a tap on the rest of the face still does, as before), and no listen starts while muted or in full quiet. The toggle is silent: a short blink and the new look, no sound. The default skin gets DefaultMouth::setSealed (a flat closed line whatever the lip sync says) and DefaultEyes::setLowered (shut whatever the emotion or the blink says), both keeping the real weight so they open again; full quiet draws the sleeping face with a small pause mark and holds it against every other emotion. The saved state is drawn once at the first standby, and a host change through self.privacy.set redraws the face (hal_bridge::privacy_face_apply). Face unmute is refused by maipai_privacy_set when the hub turned off local unmute. Needs patch 106 (maipai_privacy.h). The mint skin shapes (patches 108 and 122) are not part of this base and stay out.
# Placement: unit (the touch and the face run on the robot)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.{h,cc}, hal/board/hal_bridge.{h,cc}, stackchan/avatar/skins/default/ of the StackChan tree (MIT); new file hal/maipai_touch_core.h
# Check after a flash: tap the mouth: the eyes blink once and the mouth becomes a flat line, and the host log says 'unit privacy: ... muted=1'; tap it again and the mouth returns; tap an eye: the eyes shut; tap the forehead: the face sleeps with a small pause mark; drag from the top edge down and up for quick settings, drag left and right for volume, drag down to stop: none of these toggles anything; a tap on a cheek still starts a listen.
